An open question, stated plainly
--------------------------------

The first-party code originates with University College London, as the SGNL
Orbit Prediction Software (2017b), itself a 2014 rewrite of the pre-2010 UCL
Orbit Dynamics Library. **No copyright or licence statement existed anywhere in
the tree** - not in `README.md`, not in any file header, and there was no
`LICENSE` file. Nothing in this repository establishes who holds the rights or
who is entitled to license them.

`LICENSE` is therefore offered by the repository owner to the extent they are
entitled to do so, and it does not settle that question. Anyone intending to
rely on it for anything that matters should confirm the position with UCL
first. This file exists so that nobody discovers the ambiguity later.

